<Project>
  <!-- NuGet package metadata for miEUDIverifier.Core (used by dotnet pack) -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>miEUDIverifier.Core</PackageId>
    <!-- Baseline for local `dotnet pack`; CI overrides it from the v* tag (-p:Version=). -->
    <VersionPrefix>1.1.0</VersionPrefix>
    <Authors>Wolfgang Mitterbucher</Authors>
    <Copyright>Copyright © Wolfgang Mitterbucher</Copyright>
    <Description>Reusable .NET 8 library to read EUDI Wallet PID identity data via the EUDI Verifier Backend REST API (OpenID4VP). Builds the DCQL request (mso_mdoc and SD-JWT VC), polls for the wallet response and extracts the identity data, including SD-JWT disclosure parsing.</Description>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Mibuw/miEUDIverifier</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Mibuw/miEUDIverifier</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>eudi;eudi-wallet;eudi-verifier;openid4vp;eidas2;digital-identity;verifiable-credentials;pid;mdoc;sd-jwt;iso18013-5</PackageTags>
    <PackageReadmeFile>PACKAGE.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
1.1.0 — Multi-backend support: serve several trust ecosystems from one app.
Added VerifierSettings.Backends / DefaultBackend / MdocOnlyBackends / IntendedUseIds /
ResponseModes, the TransactionOptions type, intended_use_id on the init request, and the
German EUDI Wallet (Bundesdruckerei prototype) PID as a further SD-JWT VC option.
Note: InitializeTransactionAsync gained an optional TransactionOptions parameter ahead of
the CancellationToken. Calls passing the token by name or omitting it are unaffected;
positional InitializeTransactionAsync(ct) calls must be updated to (null, ct).
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Shown on the nuget.org package page -->
    <None Include="PACKAGE.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
